# TODO - Duplicate code detection

## Objective

Detect meaningful duplicated Rust code across project modules.

## Acceptance

- Check normalised tokens and report both source locations.
- Reject clear substantial duplicates; report uncertain near-clones.
- Exclude generated code and trivial boilerplate with explicit reasons.
- Test exact clones, near-clones and non-clones using synthetic fixtures.

## Evidence

On 2026-11-24, fresh `cargo validate --no-cache` passed after wiring
`crates/validator/src/clones.rs` into the mandatory contract gate. It
normalises Rust function-body tokens by ignoring comments and whitespace,
checks both source locations, and rejects exact substantial duplicates
across files. Body eligibility requires at least 72 tokens and four
statements to exclude trivial accessors and trait boilerplate. Renamed
structural matches are logged for manual review rather than rejected.
Generated directories, `.generated.rs` files, generated annotations, and
the ignored build/reference trees are excluded explicitly.

Synthetic tests cover exact matches, renamed near-clones, unrelated code,
trivial functions, nested comments, whitespace and raw string literals.
This is a conservative lexical gate, not a compiler-grade equivalence
proof: reordered statements, extracted helpers and semantic clones may
require separate human review.
